  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'According to the Royal Centre for Disease Control (RCDC), 154 221 cases of notifiable diseases were recorded through the weekly reporting system in 2024. RCDC also serves as the nodal point of the disease surveillance system in Bhutan.

b) Among the weekly reportable diseases, acute respiratory infections (ARI) and acute watery diarrhoea (AWD) were the most frequently reported (82.0% and 15.0% of cases in 2024). Which age group is most affected by ARI and AWD, and give up to three preventive measures for each. (2 marks)', 'b) Children under five years are most affected by both ARI and AWD (the elderly are also vulnerable to ARI). ARI prevention: hand-washing and respiratory hygiene (covering coughs, masks), vaccination (PCV, Hib, measles, influenza), exclusive breastfeeding and good nutrition, reducing indoor smoke and improving ventilation. AWD prevention: safe drinking water (boiling/chlorination), improved sanitation and hand-washing with soap, rotavirus vaccination, food hygiene and breastfeeding (with early ORS and zinc).', null, '[{"point": "Under-five children most affected (also elderly); ARI prevention: hand/respiratory hygiene, vaccination (PCV, Hib, measles, influenza), breastfeeding/ nutrition, reduce indoor smoke/ ventilation; AWD: safe water, sanitation and hand-washing, rotavirus vaccine, food hygiene, breastfeeding/ ORS-zinc", "marks": 2}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
