  values ('ME', 'passage', 'Case I: Leptospirosis outbreak in Dewathang
On 1 July 2025, the Ministry of Health issued a press release stating that "Leptospirosis Confirmed as Cause of Acute Respiratory Distress Syndrome (ARDS) Cluster in Dewathang", based on laboratory confirmation and epidemiological links.
The WHO South-East Asia Region Epidemiological Bulletin (13th edition, 2 July 2025) reported that of 230 trainees, 143 developed symptoms and were treated according to clinical protocols. Of these, three died. The Ministry has started outbreak investigation and rapid response.

a) What are the key steps in an outbreak investigation? How is a case definition developed, and why is it important? (5 + 5 marks) (10 marks)', 'Key steps: (1) prepare for fieldwork (team, logistics, permissions); (2) establish the existence of an outbreak (compare with expected numbers); (3) verify the diagnosis (clinical and laboratory); (4) construct a working case definition; (5) find and count cases systematically (line list); (6) perform descriptive epidemiology - time (epidemic curve), place (spot map) and person; (7) develop hypotheses; (8) evaluate hypotheses with analytical studies (cohort/case-control); (9) refine hypotheses and carry out laboratory and environmental studies; (10) implement control and prevention measures (as early as possible); (11) communicate findings; (12) maintain surveillance. Case definition: a standard set of criteria for deciding whether a person has the disease under investigation, made of clinical criteria (e.g. fever with myalgia and breathlessness/ARDS) restricted by time (e.g. onset after 1 June 2025), place (Dewathang training centre) and person (trainees and staff), often graded as suspected, probable and confirmed (laboratory MAT/PCR positive). It is important because it standardises counting so cases are identified consistently by all investigators, allows comparison over time and place, guides case finding and calculation of attack rates, and balances sensitivity (broad early) with specificity (narrower later).', null, '[{"point": "Steps: prepare, establish/ confirm outbreak, verify diagnosis, define and find cases, descriptive epi (time, place, person), hypotheses, test (analytical), environmental/ lab studies, control measures, communicate findings, maintain surveillance", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Case definition: clinical criteria + person, place, time restrictions; confirmed/ probable/ suspected levels; standard for counting, comparability, finding cases, sensitivity vs specificity", "marks": 5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
