d) Using the information in the scenario, write the formula and calculate the attack rate (AR) and case fatality ratio (CFR) for the leptospirosis outbreak in Dewathang. Interpret the results. (8 marks)', 'Attack rate = number of new cases during the outbreak / population at risk at the start x 100 = 143 / 230 x 100 = 62.2%. Case fatality ratio = number of deaths due to the disease / number of cases x 100 = 3 / 143 x 100 = 2.1%. Interpretation: almost two-thirds of the trainees became ill - an extremely high attack rate pointing to a common, intense exposure shared by the group (e.g. contact with water or soil contaminated by rodent urine during training). A CFR of about 2% shows the disease can be severe (pulmonary haemorrhage/ARDS), so early recognition, prompt treatment with antibiotics (doxycycline/penicillin), chemoprophylaxis for exposed people and removal of the source are essential.', null, '[{"point": "AR formula: number of new cases during outbreak / population at risk x 100", "marks": 2}, {"point": "AR = 143/230 x 100 = 62.2%", "marks": 2}, {"point": "CFR formula: deaths from disease / number of cases x 100; CFR = 3/143 x 100 = 2.1%", "marks": 2}, {"point": "Interpretation: very high attack rate - common intense exposure (e.g. contaminated water/ environment); CFR about 2% shows disease can be severe (ARDS) - need early diagnosis/ doxycycline, control", "marks": 2}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
