  values ('ME', 'passage', 'Case I: Leptospirosis outbreak in Dewathang
On 1 July 2025, the Ministry of Health issued a press release stating that "Leptospirosis Confirmed as Cause of Acute Respiratory Distress Syndrome (ARDS) Cluster in Dewathang", based on laboratory confirmation and epidemiological links.
The WHO South-East Asia Region Epidemiological Bulletin (13th edition, 2 July 2025) reported that of 230 trainees, 143 developed symptoms and were treated according to clinical protocols. Of these, three died. The Ministry has started outbreak investigation and rapid response.

f) Describe the control and prevention measures implemented during a disease outbreak in general. (10 marks)', 'Control measures act on the source, the mode of transmission and the susceptible host. (1) Control the source: identify and eliminate or treat the source (e.g. close contaminated water bodies, rodent control, safe disposal of waste, treat infected animals), and early diagnosis and treatment of cases. (2) Interrupt transmission: isolation of cases and quarantine of contacts where relevant, infection prevention and control, environmental sanitation, safe water and food, vector and rodent control, personal protective equipment (boots and gloves for leptospirosis). (3) Protect susceptible people: vaccination or mass immunisation (e.g. measles, cholera), chemoprophylaxis (e.g. weekly doxycycline for high-risk exposure), health education and risk communication. (4) Strengthen surveillance - active case finding, contact tracing, laboratory confirmation, daily reporting. (5) Coordination - rapid response teams, incident command, multisectoral (One Health) collaboration, adequate supplies and treatment protocols. (6) Monitor the effectiveness of measures, declare the end of the outbreak after two incubation periods without new cases, and conduct an after-action review to prevent recurrence.', null, '[{"point": "Control source: identify and remove/ treat source (water, food, animals/ rodents), environmental sanitation", "marks": 2.5}, {"point": "Interrupt transmission: isolation/ quarantine, infection prevention and control, vector/ rodent control, hygiene, PPE, safe water/ food", "marks": 2.5}, {"point": "Protect susceptible: vaccination, chemoprophylaxis (e.g. doxycycline), health education, risk communication", "marks": 2.5}, {"point": "Case management, surveillance, coordination (rapid response teams, incident management), monitoring effectiveness, after-action review", "marks": 2.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
