  values ('ME', 'passage', 'Case II: Non-communicable diseases
According to the World Health Organization (WHO), non-communicable diseases (NCDs) killed at least 43 million people in 2021, equivalent to 75% of non-pandemic-related deaths globally. In 2021, 18 million people died from an NCD before age 70. Of all NCD deaths, 73% are in low- and middle-income countries. Cardiovascular diseases caused at least 19 million deaths in 2021, followed by cancers (10 million), chronic respiratory diseases (COPD, 4 million) and diabetes (over 2 million, including kidney disease deaths caused by diabetes). These four groups account for 80% of all premature NCD deaths. The top causes of death in Bhutan in 2021 according to WHO are shown in Figure 1 (deaths per 100 000: ischaemic heart disease 64.6, COPD 47.9, stroke 41.1, tuberculosis 26.6, cirrhosis of the liver 19.4, diarrhoeal diseases 18.9, diabetes 18.7, lower respiratory infections 15, stomach cancer 13.1, kidney diseases 12.8).

c) (i) What characteristics of a disease indicate its suitability for screening? (4 marks)', 'Based on Wilson and Jungner''s criteria: the condition should be an important health problem (common and/or serious); it should have a recognisable latent or early symptomless stage; its natural history should be adequately understood; there should be an accepted, effective treatment that gives better outcomes when started early; there should be a suitable, simple, safe, valid (sensitive and specific) and acceptable test; facilities for diagnosis and treatment should be available; the cost of case-finding should be balanced against overall health spending; and screening should be a continuing process. Type 2 diabetes and hypertension meet these criteria.', null, '[{"point": "Wilson-Jungner criteria: important health problem (common/ serious); recognisable latent/ early stage; natural history understood; effective, acceptable treatment that is better early; suitable, acceptable, valid test; facilities for diagnosis/ treatment; cost-effective; continuous process", "marks": 4}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
