e) Describe your approach to the management of NCDs in a primary health care (PHC) setting. List the enablers and challenges of managing NCDs in PHCs. (10 marks)', 'Approach: use WHO PEN and HEARTS protocols in BHUs/PHCs - opportunistic and community screening of adults (BP, blood glucose, BMI, waist, tobacco/alcohol use), cardiovascular risk assessment; standard treatment protocols with essential medicines (antihypertensives, metformin, statins, aspirin) and basic technologies (BP machines, glucometers, urine strips); counselling on lifestyle and self-management; regular follow-up with recall systems and records in ePIS; referral of complicated cases to hospitals with back-referral; team-based care with health assistants, nurses and village health workers; community engagement and outreach for remote areas. Enablers: free health care and a wide network of PHCs; national PEN programme and standard protocols; village health workers and outreach clinics; electronic records (ePIS) and the national health flagship programmes; political commitment and GNH. Challenges: shortage and turnover of trained staff; stock-outs of medicines and test strips; difficult terrain and long travel times; low awareness, poor adherence and cultural dietary habits (salt, butter tea, alcohol); limited diagnostics and specialist support; weak data for follow-up; and rising costs.', null, '[{"point": "Approach: WHO PEN/ HEARTS protocols - screening, risk assessment, standard treatment protocols, essential drugs/ technologies, follow-up, referral, self-management, community/ VHW engagement, team-based care, records (ePIS)", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Enablers: free health care, wide PHC network, PEN implemented, VHWs, ePIS, political commitment, Health Flagship programme", "marks": 2.5}, {"point": "Challenges: shortage/ turnover of staff, drug/ equipment stock-outs, difficult terrain/ access, low awareness/ adherence, data gaps, limited specialist referral, lifestyle/ culture (diet, alcohol)", "marks": 2.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
